theorem an-exhibit-shown-by-a-trivial-line
  note        p·q is a multiple of p, n := q. The line p·q = p·q shows the
              reader the value by comparing it with the body, and is used,
              though the equation would name its value itself.
  let p ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  let q ∈ ℕ                                                           (H2)
  then there is n ∈ ℕ with p·q = p·n

1.  p·q = p·q
    algebra

2.  There is n ∈ ℕ with p·q = p·n.
    exhibit, from 1
